-- title:
--   Noetherian approximation for proper flat morphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, let $A$ be a commutative $A_0$-algebra (both in a fixed universe), let $X$ be a scheme and let $g\colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ be a morphism of schemes which is proper, flat and locally of finite presentation. Let $s$ be a finite subset of $A$. Then there exists an $A_0$-subalgebra $T \subseteq A$ which is finitely generated as an $A_0$-algebra (`Subalgebra.FG`) and contains $s$, together with a scheme $X_0$, a morphism $f_0\colon X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} T$ and a morphism $\pi\colon X \to X_0$, such that $f_0$ is proper, $f_0$ is flat, and the square with horizontal edges $\pi$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $T \hookrightarrow A$ and vertical edges $g$ and $f_0$ is cartesian; that is, $\pi$ and $g$ exhibit $X$ as the fibre product $X_0 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} T} \operatorname{Spec} A$. Note that $T$ is only asserted to be of finite type over $A_0$, hence Noetherian since $A_0$ is, not to be one of the subalgebras generated by any prescribed further data.
--
--   This is absolute Noetherian approximation for proper flat morphisms: a proper, flat, locally finitely presented scheme over an arbitrary ring is the base change of a proper flat scheme over a ring of finite type over a given Noetherian base (Grothendieck, EGA IV₃, 8.9.1, 8.10.5, 11.2.6). It is used in the project to reduce statements about proper flat morphisms over general rings to the Noetherian case, for instance in the corresponding approximation statements for closed immersions into projective space and for finite morphisms, and in the analysis of global sections of proper flat schemes over a local ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_fg_subalgebra_isProper_flat_isPullback_of_isProper_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation.lean

import Mathlib

